    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7afc3694_d36cced4",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-10T10:15:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Wifi P2P is local only, so it should not be restricted by entitlement.",
      "parentUuid": "ee098ab2_d114c491",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a1d7bf81_d3c6c8fe",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-11T08:35:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sure, but IIUC, with the current code, it will. UpstreamMonitor doesn\u0027t stop to think about whether the downstream in P2P and just notifies of upstream changes. When startTethering() is called with TETHERING_WIFI_P2P, it will trigger the entitlement check if cellular happens to be the default network, even if it\u0027s not going to be used.\n\nAm I missing something ?",
      "parentUuid": "7afc3694_d36cced4",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbe2dc23_a2e1de43",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-11T08:53:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It would not trigger entitlement because P2P don\u0027t call #startTethering to tell EntitlementManager that TETHERING_WIFI_P2P need provisioning. And cellular upstream would be restricted in this case. And it is fine because wifi P2P already claim it is local only(refer Tethering.java line.825) which means wifi P2P would not request upstream(Tethering#upstreamWanted() would return false).\n\nNormal tethering enable flow: Settings -\u003e Tethering#startTethering() -\u003e WifiManager#startSoftap() -\u003e wifi send intent to tell tethering wifi driver is ready.\nHow wifi P2P start tethering ? No #startTethering(), wifi p2p just send the intent to tell tethering p2p driver is ready. Only local only mode is allowed to use this way.",
      "parentUuid": "a1d7bf81_d3c6c8fe",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d4bc3ef1_27a4be69",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1322948
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-12T08:38:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Normally, this type is not invoked from startTethering. It should not notify entitlement app, there is nothing to shown for this on status bar.",
      "parentUuid": "ee098ab2_d114c491",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "abb417a4_49533430",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T02:37:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It sounds rather obscure to me that this difference is baked into the call graph rather than enforced in the relevant parts in the code. I take on board that p2p will never need entitlement because it never has an upstream, but I think this should be enforced by checks against upstreams rather than rely on the fact that today p2p never calls #startTethering. Hopefully in the future all tethering technologies will follow the same code path and I expect nobody will remember p2p needs this special case ; I think the code needs to not cause damage if someone makes it so that p2p starts calling #startTethering some time in the future.\n\nDo we already test for the presence of an upstream ? Or do we have checks for local-only hotspots enforcing this ? If we don\u0027t I think we should build that in this change – hopefully it\u0027s only one or two lines of code.",
      "parentUuid": "d4bc3ef1_27a4be69",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "10eb97b6_305a6c27",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1308504
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T04:15:17Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agree with you that all tethering follow the same code patch would be better, but this would not happen in R time frame because it need existing 3rd party APP(using local only hotspot, P2P,....) change to call #startTethering().\nIn entitlement design, if upstream don\u0027t check entitlement it would be treat as provisioning denied implicitly.\n\nI think we don\u0027t for the presence of an upstream even for local only hotspot, but it is very easy to test. We just need to add few lines as below for testing(Tracking in b/142292441).\nIn TetheringTest.java\nverify(mUpstreamNetworkMonitor, never()).getCurrentPreferredUpstream();\nverify(mUpstreamNetworkNonitor, never()).selectPreferredUpstreamType(any());",
      "parentUuid": "abb417a4_49533430",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
