    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bdb955a7_ad71005e",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1322948
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-08T06:42:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Current Wifi, Usb, and Bt tethering, they need to start from startTethering because this is the entry point of the function and the role is known.\n\nFor P2p, the entry point is p2p-pairing and the role is known in the middle of the whole p2p flow, not the beginning.\nI could still call startTethering after knowing the role, but there is nothing to do for Tethering, just a notification. Do you want this? This is still different from wifi/usb/bt cases unless we change the whole p2p flow from Settings.\n\nIn current design, if someone still call startTethering with TETHER_WIFI_P2P, it fails immediately with TETHER_ERROR_UNKNOWN_IFACE since there is no case for this type.\n\nI add upstream tests as Mark said for p2p tethering.",
      "parentUuid": "abb417a4_49533430",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "49e11fc2_004fc733",
        "filename": "core/java/android/net/ConnectivityManager.java",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 481,
      "author": {
        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-10-17T09:02:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "In any case I\u0027m not asking you to completely rehaul the architecture in this patch. I would like all upstreams to work in the same way ultimately, but that\u0027s an end goal.\n\nI think with Mark\u0027s suggestion we are in a better place though I meant testing for the thing in the main code – test coverage is never as high as you really think it is. But for now I think it\u0027s fine. In any case, with this the code certainly clears the \"make the codebase better than it used to be\" bar that it needs for +2 :)",
      "parentUuid": "bdb955a7_ad71005e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 481,
        "startChar": 28,
        "endLine": 481,
        "endChar": 46
      },
      "revId": "79ceeec47da94c24ea19e07ca54922f2e1f8e6de",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
